WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:15.181
next morning everyone was awake early.

2
00:00:15.921 --> 00:00:20.485
The children sprang about the tree house like monkeys while I sat beneath the great tree.

3
00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:22.907
"What should we do next, Father?"

4
00:00:23.247 --> 00:00:24.448
Franz called down to me.

5
00:00:25.349 --> 00:00:27.090
"What do you want us to do today?"

6
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.993
"Rest, my boys," I replied.

7
00:00:30.013 --> 00:00:32.895
"Rest." "Rest?"

8
00:00:33.195 --> 00:00:33.956
Franz repeated.

9
00:00:34.332 --> 00:00:35.532
"Why should we rest?"

10
00:00:35.552 --> 00:00:37.013
"It's Sunday.

11
00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:38.273
Come down here, please."

12
00:00:38.293 --> 00:00:42.194
"Is it really Sunday?"

13
00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.455
asked Jack when he'd climbed down the ladder.

14
00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:45.996
"How jolly!

15
00:00:46.376 --> 00:00:47.516
I won't do any work.

16
00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:50.797
I'll take a bow and arrow and prowl through the woods.

17
00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.058
And we'll climb about the tree and have fun all day."

18
00:00:54.078 --> 00:00:57.119
"That's not resting, Jack," I pointed out.

19
00:00:57.139 --> 00:01:00.420
"That's not the way you usually spend Sundays."

20
00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:04.133
"I usually go to church, but we don't have a church here."

21
00:01:04.153 --> 00:01:08.834
"And we don't have a clergyman or an organ," added little Franz.

22
00:01:09.674 --> 00:01:12.315
"We can still offer thanks for our new home," I said.

23
00:01:12.335 --> 00:01:14.956
"Come, everyone, gather around me."

24
00:01:16.096 --> 00:01:20.097
After I led my family in some prayers and hymns, the boys were free to do as they

25
00:01:20.137 --> 00:01:23.018
liked. I continued to sit under our tree.

26
00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:27.619
A few birds came to feed on the figs, which were just beginning to ripen.

27
00:01:28.419 --> 00:01:32.401
I realized that as more figs ripened, more birds would come.

28
00:01:33.241 --> 00:01:37.684
If we could preserve some birds, we could eat them during the rainy season when food might be

29
00:01:37.744 --> 00:01:43.767
scarce. Relieved that I'd thought of a way to provide food for my family, I enjoyed my morning

30
00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:44.327
in the shade.

31
00:01:45.168 --> 00:01:49.170
During lunch I proposed that we name all the places we'd visited since we arrived.

32
00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:53.493
"We'll feel more at home if these places have names," I said.

33
00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.574
"Let's start by naming the bay where we landed."

34
00:01:57.775 --> 00:01:59.076
"Oyster Bay," said Fritz.

35
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.881
"No, no," protested Jack.

36
00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:05.923
"Lobster Bay, in memory of the fellow who grabbed my leg."

37
00:02:06.744 --> 00:02:09.565
"I think we should call it Safety Bay," said my wife.

38
00:02:10.406 --> 00:02:13.908
"It will be a token of our gratitude for a safe escape from the ship."

39
00:02:15.049 --> 00:02:15.589
"I like it!"

40
00:02:15.909 --> 00:02:16.489
said Ernest.

41
00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:21.212
The others agreed, and so the bay was known as Safety Bay from that moment on.

42
00:02:21.992 --> 00:02:25.314
We easily decided on Tentholm for the place where we first lived.

43
00:02:26.175 --> 00:02:31.153
Many names were proposed for our tree house, but we finally decided on Falconhurst.

44
00:02:32.213 --> 00:02:33.933
We spent the rest of the day quietly.

45
00:02:37.755 --> 00:02:40.495
The following morning I proposed an expedition to Tentholm.

46
00:02:42.376 --> 00:02:43.596
We went by a different route.

47
00:02:44.336 --> 00:02:46.217
The boys roamed ahead of my wife and me.

48
00:02:47.017 --> 00:02:49.578
Knips the monkey rode along on Juno the dog.

49
00:02:50.438 --> 00:02:56.200
Soon I heard a joyful shout, and Ernest came running toward me at full speed, followed by his

50
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.541
brothers. He held out a plant for me to see.

51
00:02:59.561 --> 00:03:02.423
"Potatoes! Potatoes, Father!"

52
00:03:02.684 --> 00:03:03.985
Ernest was gasping for breath.

53
00:03:04.005 --> 00:03:06.086
"Yes," said Jack.

54
00:03:06.106 --> 00:03:08.168
"Acres and acres of potatoes.

55
00:03:08.908 --> 00:03:09.589
Come look at them."

56
00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.251
My wife and I hurried to the spot.

57
00:03:13.051 --> 00:03:16.854
There indeed was a great area of land covered with potato plants.

58
00:03:18.335 --> 00:03:20.937
"Ernest, you've made a great discovery," I said.

59
00:03:20.957 --> 00:03:24.580
"With all these potatoes, we'll always have something to eat."

60
00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.703
"Ernest may have the honor of discovering the potatoes," said Jack.

61
00:03:28.723 --> 00:03:32.447
"But I'll have the honor of being the first to harvest them."

62
00:03:33.287 --> 00:03:35.730
So he set to work digging potatoes with his hands.

63
00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:40.274
Knips followed his example and soon had a pile of potatoes beside him.

64
00:03:41.274 --> 00:03:46.559
Everyone began digging, and we didn't stop until we'd filled every bag, pouch, and pocket.

65
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.644
We pushed on to Tentholm, loaded down with potatoes but happy with our find.

66
00:03:52.488 --> 00:03:57.029
Along the way the boys pestered me for the names and uses of the many strange plants and

67
00:03:57.109 --> 00:03:58.070
trees we passed.

68
00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.951
I recognized some of them, but there were many others that I couldn't identify.

69
00:04:03.751 --> 00:04:08.092
Everything was safe at Tentholm, and we began gathering what we wanted to take back.

70
00:04:09.053 --> 00:04:12.654
I collected a fresh supply of salt, and my wife wanted to make butter.

71
00:04:13.714 --> 00:04:18.195
Jack and Ernest ran down to the beach to capture the geese and ducks that we'd left behind.

72
00:04:18.955 --> 00:04:22.889
The birds were out on the water, and nothing could persuade them to come ashore.

73
00:04:22.909 --> 00:04:24.190
"I know!"

74
00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:25.131
said Ernest.

75
00:04:25.151 --> 00:04:27.832
"Let's ask Mother for some cheese and string."

76
00:04:27.852 --> 00:04:30.274
"Cheese and string?"

77
00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:31.174
said Jack.

78
00:04:31.194 --> 00:04:32.395
"Who will eat that?"

79
00:04:32.415 --> 00:04:37.258
"Just watch," said Ernest as he led Jack to the tent for supplies.

80
00:04:38.118 --> 00:04:43.081
Back at the beach, the boys broke off pieces of cheese and tied a long string around each

81
00:04:43.241 --> 00:04:48.124
one. Ernest threw the bait into the water, and the hungry birds instantly went after it.

82
00:04:49.056 --> 00:04:54.759
With a little maneuvering, he got the birds onshore, where Jack caught them and tied their feet together.

83
00:04:55.759 --> 00:04:57.620
We soon set off for Falconhurst.

84
00:04:59.741 --> 00:05:02.503
After a pleasant walk, we were back at our tree house.

85
00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.204
I released the birds into our stream.

86
00:05:06.085 --> 00:05:09.947
After a delicious supper of potatoes, milk, and butter, we went to bed.
